.Dd $Mdocdate: October 12 2026 $
.Dt TARSNAP.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tarsnap.conf
.Fo
.Nm
\-= configuration file
.Fc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm tarsnap
.Rs
Reads configuration from
.Pa @sysconfdir@/tarsnap.conf
and
.Pa ~/.tarsnaprc .
.Re
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm tarsnap
configuration file is a simple text file containing one option per
line.
A line beginning with the character
.Ql #
is treated as a comment.
Options are specified as name\-value pairs, separated by a single space
character.
For options that do not accept a value (flags), only the name is
specified.
The following options may be specified:
.It Cm gzip-compression Ar X
.It Cm maxbw
.It Cm maxbw-rate-down
.It Cm maxbw-rate-up
.It Cm noatime
.It Cm nodump
.It Cm normalmem
.It Cm no-aggressive-networking
.It Cm no-backup-metadata
.It Cm no-compression-sample
.It Cm no-cpupri
.It Cm no-debug
.It Cm no-force-tar
.It Cm no-list-all-keyfiles
.It Cm no-print-stats
.It Cm no-quiet
.It Cm no-retry-forever
.It Cm no-snaptime
.It Cm no-store-atime
.It Cm no-totals
.It Cm passphrase Ar method:arg
.It Cm print-stats
.It Cm progress-bytes Ar X
.It Cm quiet
.It Cm retry-forever
.It Cm snaptime Pa file
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa @sysconfdir@/tarsnap.conf
System-wide configuration file.
.It Pa ~/.tarsnaprc
User-specific configuration file.
.El
.Sh NOTES
Note that the
.Cm no-*
options can override settings from lower-priority configuration files when
specified in
.Pa ~/.tarsnaprc ,
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tarsnap/tarsnap.conf ,
or
.Pa ~/.config/tarsnap/tarsnap.conf .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr tarsnap 1
.Sh AUTHOR
.An Ian Goldberg aMtian@cse.uwaterloo.ca\a
<<<END_PR_DESCRIPTION>>>
## Summary
Two `tarsnap.conf(5)` documentation corrections:

1. **Added five accepted options to the explicit list** — `noatime`, `no-noatime`, `progress-bytes`, `no-progress-bytes`, and `passphrase` were accepted by the parser but absent from both manual page formats (`tarsnap.conf.5-man.in` and `tarsnap.conf.5-mdoc.in`).

2. **Updated the description of negating options to account for XDG configuration** — replaced the too-narrow sentence that only mentioned `~/.tarsnaprc` with the correct per-user precedence that also includes `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tarsnap/tarsnap.conf` and `~/.config/tarsnap/tarsnap.conf`.

Closes #995
/attempt
/claim #995

